hexagonrpc (0.4.0-0marble1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Independently build upstream hexagonrpc 0.4.0 for the Ubuntu 24.04
    device-package baseline. Ubuntu noble does not package hexagonrpcd,
    which leaves the SSC sensor stack (libssc + iio-sensor-proxy-ssc)
    without its FastRPC daemon. Debian trixie/forky/sid and Ubuntu
    resolute/stonking already provide an archive package, so the rootfs
    installer keeps the distribution copy there and uses this one only
    where the archive has no candidate.
  * Ship the Debian-compatible hexagonrpcd wrapper, systemd service, udev
    rule and the real daemon under /usr/libexec/hexagonrpc. The wrapper
    keeps the hexagonrpcd_device/_dsp/_fw_dir overrides used by
    marble-device-support.

